;; FH-TOPLAYER-004 — the commit law, the tracking frequency, and the exact
;; cleanup count.
;;
;; Three claims that are only worth anything as EXACT integers, so this row
;; asserts integers:
;;
;;   1. Building elements performs ZERO host operations. The host call rides
;;      a React ref, and React runs a ref only for a render it committed, so
;;      an abandoned candidate's desired state cannot reach the browser. A
;;      detach performs zero as well, and does more than nothing: it RETIRES
;;      that generation, withdrawing the operation it still had waiting in
;;      the checkpoint. Ownership is the fence, not connectivity — a
;;      generation retires while its node stays in the document whenever a
;;      commit removes the intrinsic without removing the element — and a
;;      retirement never withdraws a SUCCESSOR's claim on the same node.
;;   2. Re-committing an UNCHANGED desired state performs zero further
;;      operations. The diff is read from the live node, so a repeated equal
;;      value is a no-op however many times the parent re-renders — and a
;;      browser-initiated dismissal is visible to that same diff, which is
;;      why remembered state was not used.
;;   3. Mounting, opening, closing and unmounting arms NOTHING that outlives
;;      the cycle: no document or window listener, no ResizeObserver,
;;      IntersectionObserver or MutationObserver, no interval. The deltas are
;;      counted against instrumented globals and every one of them must be
;;      exactly zero — a leak here compounds per open/close cycle, which is
;;      precisely the failure the top layer exists to delete.
;;
;; `:renders` is how many extra commits the unchanged-state case performs.
;; More than one, so a per-render host call would show up as a count rather
;; than as a coincidence.
{:fh/id "FH-TOPLAYER-004"
 :fh/law
 "Host work happens only at a selected commit and only when the desired state differs from the node's live state: building elements and detaching perform zero operations, a detach RETIRES its generation — withdrawing that generation's pending operation even while its node stays connected, and never a successor's — N re-commits of an unchanged desired state perform zero further operations, and a full mount/open/close/unmount cycle leaves exactly zero retained listeners, observers, intervals and pending batch entries."

 :menu-id "account-menu"
 :renders 3

 :instrumented
 ["document.addEventListener"
  "window.addEventListener"
  "ResizeObserver"
  "IntersectionObserver"
  "MutationObserver"
  "setInterval"]}
